## Summary

An expanded outline group draws its bracket while any of its first 4096 detail lines is on screen, and draws no bracket once the view has moved entirely past those lines. The same thing happens for a column group. Cell values and outline levels stay as they were, and the level buttons in the band corner stay on screen. The missing piece is the bracket stroke for a group longer than 4096 lines.

## Steps to reproduce

On the baseline, create one expanded level-1 group over row indexes 0 through 4999, which are spreadsheet rows 1 through 5000. Its summary line is index 5000. The fixture sets stored outline levels directly and does not click the ribbon. At a viewport of 800 by 600 points, compare the bracket at scroll line 4095 with lines 4096, 4200 and 4970. Repeat for a 5000-column group at lines 4095, 4096 and 4200. The fixture records all samples before either test asserts.

