## Summary

Opening an `.xlsx` sheet whose single hyperlink list covers more than 10,000 cells keeps hyperlinks for only the first 10,000 cells and drops the rest. This writer emits one list per sheet, which is the case that was run. The read succeeds with an empty warning list. Saving afterward writes only kept links. All cell values remain. A separate hyperlink list starts a new count, so this is not an aggregate sheet-wide limit.

## Steps to reproduce

Use the baseline named under Runtime or environment. Create one sheet, put text in A1:A12000, and put an internal hyperlink on each of those cells (`Sheet1!B1` on A1 through `Sheet1!B12000` on A12000). Write the workbook to `.xlsx` bytes and read those bytes back. Then write the workbook that came back and read that second package. For the range form, read a worksheet whose only hyperlink element is `<hyperlink ref="A1:A12000" location="x"/>`, with a styles part present so a missing stylesheet is not confused with this skip. Read a three-link sheet of the same shape as the control.

