## Summary

CSV export builds the entire used-range rectangle in memory without a cell or byte budget. Two cells far apart can therefore require gigabytes of output even though the workbook stores only two one-character values. This violates the repository's explicit requirement to cap input-sized allocations for huge ranges. Small exports preserve their values and positions; the defect is the missing resource bound for large valid ranges.

## Steps to reproduce

Use the source checkout identified under Runtime or environment. Add the following bounded integration test as `crates/engine/tests/repro_csv_range_budget.rs`. It writes no export files and tests the supported in-memory CSV command plus the serializer shared by file export.

