## Summary

For matched numeric arrays whose probabilities total one, `PROB` accepts a probability of zero and returns a number. Microsoft's documented rule for this existing Excel-targeted function requires `#NUM!` when any probability is zero. Callers receive a normal result instead of the documented invalid-input signal, including when the zero-probability outcome lies outside the requested interval.

