## Summary

Searching for empty text in "abc" with start position 4 returns the number 4 from both FIND and SEARCH. Their adopted Excel contract requires #VALUE! when the start position exceeds the text length. This gives dependent calculations a successful numeric result where they should receive an error. The failure reproduced through the function library's public dispatcher with ordinary scalar arguments.

## Steps to reproduce

Use the source baseline and toolchain under Runtime or environment. The following package-level reproduction invokes the same public function dispatcher used by the calculation engine. It needs no workbook or external application.

1. Create `crates/functions/tests/find_empty_start.rs` with this integration test. The assertions deliberately check the documented error result for the two failing cases.

