`apply_filter` currently recognizes only `Value::Empty`. Formula `=""` evaluates to `Value::Text("")`; imported empty shared strings have that representation too. The dropdown also treats empty text separately from `(Blanks)`.

A proposed local fix uses one filter-specific predicate for `Empty` and zero-length `Text` in application and dropdown grouping. It does not trim whitespace or change `Value::is_empty`, formula storage, or Go To Special `blanks`. Synthetic XLSX round-trip tests cover missing cells, stored empty text, `=""`, space/tab/NBSP, zero, dropdown deduplication, undo and redo; both tests fail before the fix and pass after it.

