A command-sequence fuzz run (seed 1688, `GRIDCRAFT_FUZZ_STEPS=200`) fails the full-recalc invariant: a cell holds a value in memory that is empty after a full recalculation. It reproduces on main (0.9.0) with five commands.

Starting from `file.new {"sample": "grades"}`:

```
home.mergeCells {"range":"F:H"}
cell.set {"cell":"J54","input":"=SEQUENCE(5)*C6"}
selection.set {"range":"15:15"}
sheet.move {"copy":true,"sheet":0,"to":1}
cell.set {"array":true,"cell":"D3","input":"=SUM('Q4 2026'!J54#)"}
```

Result on main: on the copied sheet `Grades (2)`, cell J55 holds `190` in memory and is empty after a full recalc. (On the branch I was working on the same sequence names J48 on the copy instead; the sheet and cell depend on the build, the failure is the same.)

Replay the original run: `GRIDCRAFT_FUZZ_SEED=1688 GRIDCRAFT_FUZZ_STEPS=200 GRIDCRAFT_FUZZ_SHRINK=1 cargo test -p gridcraft-engine --test command_sequence_fuzz`

I have not looked for the cause. J55 sits inside the spill of `=SEQUENCE(5)*C6` in J54, so it may be related to #964 (a spill area changing hands on a recalc). It does not involve paste: it came up while fixing a paste crash on the same seed (#2018), which had hidden it.

