Fub edits `.xlsx` files with GridCraft and saves them back. To keep a save from rewriting what the user did not touch, we carry a large patch on v0.11.1 (about 3,200 lines with tests) that writes each unchanged object in the form the file stored it:

- rich-text runs in cells and shared strings;
- notes with their VML shapes;
- x14 data validations and conditional formats;
- drawings and charts;
- styles (fonts, fills, borders, dxfs) and `sheetView` attributes and workbook extensions.

The reader keeps the source form next to the model value, and the writer reuses it when the model value is unchanged; an edited object is written as today. Files written by Excel and LibreOffice then come back byte-identical in the parts nobody edited, and a second save is a no-op.

It does not rebase cleanly on `main` any more (the reader hardening touched the same code), so before redoing it I would like to know whether you want it, and in which shape: one PR per object kind, in the order above, each with its round-trip tests. Related: #2137, #1490, #1209.

